{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpYwzb8ytasVxVuHN7XwK4","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t                         renaming ( refl to refl₂ ; sym to sym₂ ; trans to trans₂ )\n41\t\n42\t  open _⟶_ {a = α}{ρᵃ}{β}{ρᵇ}{From = 𝑨}{To = 𝑩} renaming (to to _⟨$⟩_ )\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\t\n46\tWe begin by defining two data types that represent the semantic concept of the\n47\t*image* of a function.  The first of these is for functions on bare types, while\n48\tthe second is for functions on setoids.\n49\t\n50\t\n51\t```agda\n52\t  data Img_∋_ (f : A → B) : B → Type (α ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ) where\n53\t    eq : {b : B} → (a : A) → b ≈₂ (f a) → Img f ∋ b\n54\t\n55\t\n56\t  data Image_∋_ (F : 𝑨 ⟶ 𝑩) : B → Type (α ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ) where\n57\t    eq : {b : B} → (a : A) → b ≈₂ (F ⟨$⟩ a) → Image F ∋ b\n58\t\n59\t  open Image_∋_\n60\t\n61\t  IsInRange : (𝑨 ⟶ 𝑩) → Pred B (α ⊔ ρᵇ)\n62\t  IsInRange F b = ∃[ a ∈ A ] (F ⟨$⟩ a) ≈₂ b\n63\t\n64\t  Image⊆Range : ∀ {F b} → Image F ∋ b → b ∈ IsInRange F\n65\t  Image⊆Range (eq a x) = a , (sym₂ x)\n66\t\n67\t  IsInRange→IsInImage : ∀ {F b} → b ∈ IsInRange F → Image F ∋ b\n68\t  IsInRange→IsInImage (a , x) = eq a (sym₂ x)\n69\t\n70\t  Imagef∋f : ∀ {F a} → Image F ∋ (F ⟨$⟩ a)\n71\t  Imagef∋f = eq _ refl₂\n72\t\n73\t  -- Alternative representation of the range of a Func as a setoid\n74\t\n75\t  -- the carrier\n76\t  range : (𝑨 ⟶ 𝑩) → Type (α ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ)\n77\t  range F = Σ[ b ∈ B ] ∃[ a ∈ A ] (F ⟨$⟩ a) ≈₂ b\n78\t\n79\t  image : (F : 𝑨 ⟶ 𝑩) → range F → B\n80\t  image F (b , (_ , _)) = b\n81\t\n82\t  preimage : (F : 𝑨 ⟶ 𝑩) → range F → A\n83\t  preimage F (_ , (a , _)) = a\n84\t\n85\t  f∈range : ∀ {F} → A → range F\n86\t  f∈range {F} a = (F ⟨$⟩ a) , (a , refl₂)\n87\t\n88\t  ⌜_⌝ : (F : 𝑨 ⟶ 𝑩) → A → range F\n89\t  ⌜ F ⌝ a = f∈range{F} a"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3b51d98-8556-415b-8140-80ba327a0b07","uuid":"a4087024-ecef-490a-a24b-f7e3e768a441","timestamp":"2026-09-29T07:23:53.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","